      "text": "To solve for the $y$-intercepts, we set $x=0$ in the equation\n\\[x = 2y^2 - 6y + 3\\]. This gives\n\\[2y^2 - 6y + 3 = 0.\\]\nThus,\n\\[y=\\left(a,0\\right)=\\frac{6 \\pm \\sqrt{36 - 4 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3}}{4}= \\frac{6 \\pm \\sqrt{12}}{4} =\\frac{6 \\pm 2 \\sqrt{3}}{4} \\Rightarrow \\left(a,0\\right)=\\left(\\frac{6+2 \\sqrt{3}}{4},0\\right) \\text{ or } \\left(1,0\\right).\\]\nSo $a=1$.\nFor the $x$-intercept, we set $y=0$ in the equation. This gives\n\\[x = -3.\\]\nThus, $b=-3$ or $c=-3$.\n\nTo find $a+b+c$, we need to find $1 + (-3) + (-3)$.  This simplifies to\n\\[a + b + c = 1 - 3 - 3 = \\boxed{-5}.\\]. The answer is -5",
